Chapter 22
A song leads Bao-yu to an insight into Chan;
Lantern riddles sadden Jia Zheng with words of ill omen

‘Now that really is complete enlightenment,’ said Bao-chai. ‘Long ago Hui-neng, the Sixth Patriarch of the Southern School, came to Shaozhou when he first went in search of a teacher. Hearing that the Fifth Patriarch, Hong-ren, was at Huangmei, he went to serve as a kitchen monk. The Fifth Patriarch wanted to choose a successor to his teaching, so he ordered each of his disciples to compose a verse. The senior monk, Shen-xiu, said:
“The body is the bodhi tree;
The heart is like a stand for a bright mirror.
Diligently wipe it, time after time;
Let no dust remain.”
